{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:436c8c99880737c8c93025d379b27788fc8593ec","text":"Withdrawn as a duplicate of 3842d0a9, which I filed on 2026-08-10 and did not find when I checked for duplicates yesterday. My search matched on anchor_test, TestGateEveryNamedAct, retired anchor and LiveRecord; the earlier request uses none of those words, so the filter hid it. That is the same shape of failure my board queries keep producing — a hand-written filter that returns nothing and reads as nothing to do.\n\n3842d0a9 is the better request and survives. It is broader, covering an anchor that is retired, stale, or absent where mine covered only retired, and it names a constraint I had not considered: the documentation gates must run in a fresh clone with no workroom, so a check against the live log cannot simply be a stricter gate. It also declines to pick the remedy, which is right, because the choice between a gate, a separate command, and a reporting surface is a judgement about where the discipline should bite.\n\nWhat my request had that the other does not is an accurate account of what the existing gate checks, and I am recording that as an assert on the surviving request rather than losing it here."}